Start
/ task: a call in parallel answers a task; a later step waits for it or cancels it. Each stage is a goal; each
/ behaviour a comment with the test that proves it. The coder rewrites each test in plang that compiles.
- call goal Stage1
- call goal Stage2
- call goal Stage3

Stage1
/ The task and the call.
/ A call in parallel answers a task, and the next step runs before the called goal ends
- call goal /module/goal/call/ParallelAnswersATask
/ A plain call still waits and answers the goal's result (Parallel is false by default)
- call goal /module/goal/call/PlainCallWaits
/ A running task is in %!app.actor.current.task.list%; once it ends it isn't, and %task% still holds it
- call goal /module/goal/call/TaskListedWhileRunning
/ A task that fails with nobody waiting is reported on its actor's error channel
- call goal /module/goal/call/UnwatchedFailureReported
/ The llm tool loop runs two Parallel tools as tasks and waits for both (C# pin in the tool-call harness)
- call goal /module/goal/call/ToolLoopRunsTasks

Stage2
/ The task module.
/ wait for %task% answers the goal's result
- call goal /module/task/wait/WaitAnswersResult
/ wait for %a%, %b% answers a list of their results, in order
- call goal /module/task/wait/WaitForSeveral
/ wait for %tasks% (a list of tasks) answers their results, in order
- call goal /module/task/wait/WaitForList
/ A failed task fails the wait step; on error handles it
- call goal /module/task/wait/FailedTaskFailsWait
/ A failure reported while nobody waited is still the answer of a later wait
- call goal /module/task/wait/LateWaitGetsFailure
/ cancel %task% stops it: a write its goal makes after a sleep never happens
- call goal /module/task/cancel/CancelStops
/ cancel %task%, write to %result%: the result when the task had already ended, null when the cancel stopped it
- call goal /module/task/cancel/CancelAnswer
/ wait for a cancelled task fails as Cancelled
- call goal /module/task/cancel/WaitOnCancelledFails

Stage3
/ The builder (built goldens, measured fresh).
/ "call X in parallel, write to %t%" builds Parallel=true
- call goal /module/goal/call/build/InParallel
/ "call X, don't wait" and "call X in the background" build Parallel=true
- call goal /module/goal/call/build/DontWait
/ "call X" builds no Parallel
- call goal /module/goal/call/build/Plain
/ "wait for %t%, write to %r%" builds task.wait, and "wait 2 seconds" still builds timer.sleep
- call goal /module/task/build/WaitNotSleep
